# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build outputs
dist/
.next/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Turbo
.turbo/

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Debug / Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
*.log

# Coverage
coverage/

# SQL files — scratch dumps, not schema.
*.sql
**/*.sql
# ...except the schema itself, which SHIPS.
#
# ADD A NEW SCHEMA FILE HERE OR THE BUILD BREAKS ON A CLEAN CLONE, silently on
# the machine that wrote it. baseschema.sql is //go:embed-ed, so leaving it out
# is not a missing file at runtime — it is `pattern baseschema.sql: no matching
# files found` for whoever clones, and nothing on the author's machine says so.
!apps/system/internal/store/baseschema.sql
!tools/schema/*.sql

# Test files
# NO TEST EXCLUSIONS. These patterns used to live here and were a trap: a
# contributor adding foo.test.ts would find `git add -A` silently skipping it,
# with nothing saying why. Keeping tests out of the PUBLISHED package is a
# different job and package.json's `files` allowlist already does it.

# Private keys and certificates. gitleaks runs over the full history in CI and is
# the real gate; this is so a mistake is caught before it becomes a commit at all.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.crx
**/test/
**/tests/
# ...except the guard's conformance suite. It is not a dev scratch dir: it is the
# contract any reimplementation has to pass, so it ships with the source.
!packages/proxy/test/
!packages/proxy/test/**

# Shell scripts (dev/test only)
**/*.sh

# ...except the installer, which is the first thing anybody runs.
#
# This rule swallowed it silently. `git add -A` skips an ignored file without a
# word, so install.sh was written, made executable, tested on a fresh clone, and
# committed in a change whose message described adding it — and it was never in
# the repository. The clone it was written for did not have it.
!/install.sh

# ...and the test runner, for the same reason and with the same failure waiting:
# CONTRIBUTING.md tells every contributor to run `./test.sh`, and a clone without
# it reads as the instructions being wrong.
!/test.sh

# Icon/Logo files (served from CDN)
**/public/icon-*.png
**/public/apple-icon.png
**/public/favicon.ico
**/public/solongate-logo.png

# Deploy packages
deploy-package/

*.md
# ...except the ones that are documentation rather than scratch notes. The blanket
# rule above exists to keep stray AI/plan files out; these are meant to ship.
#
# ADD A NEW DOC HERE OR IT IS INVISIBLE. The blanket rule is silent: `git add`
# refuses without being asked, `git status` does not list the file, and the first
# anybody notices is a clone with no README in it.
!README.md
!packages/proxy/test/README.md

# The open source release set: the files people look for before they look at code.
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!SECURITY.md

# The GitHub issue templates, for the markdown ones.
!.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*.md
# Lock files (pnpm only)
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

